Feature: Proposer doors for the bounded loop
  A proposer may submit expressions, sketches with holes and family programs.
  The doors propose; transform check and its receipt replay decide every acceptance.
  Regions, repair sites, unrealizable and not-found are the doors' own untrusted findings.

  @stage-1
  @atdd-loop-doors-repair
  Scenario: Explain a wrong expression with its failing region and ranked sites and return a checked repair
    Given a loop session on an exported core program and one expression per output with a wrong constant
    When the expression door spends one attempt and the session's check finds a counterexample
    Then the failing region counts exactly the tuples where the proposal is wrong
    And the top repair site is the wrong constant in the proposer's own text
    And the repair is labelled a checked repair only after transform check accepts it and its receipt replays
    And a fault at the root of an output is repaired by its one-step edit

  @stage-1
  @atdd-loop-doors-sketch
  Scenario: Complete a sketch's holes and check the completion through the session
    Given a sketch with three constant holes in one output and the other outputs kept
    When the sketch door solves the holes
    Then the holes complete to the constants that make every tuple right
    And the completion passes the session's check and an in-process transform check whose receipt replays
    And a search stopped by its budget is inconclusive and spends no attempt

  @stage-1
  @atdd-loop-doors-unrealizable
  Scenario: Report an unrealizable sketch only with a witness input or an exhausted complete space
    Given a sketch whose single hole sits in a branch that is never taken where the output is wrong
    When the sketch door solves it
    Then the sketch is unrealizable with a witness input that the independent reference confirms
    And an exhausted claim lists a complete candidate space that the reference enumerates
    And the reference rejects planted false claims and accepts them only when its comparison is stubbed

  @stage-1
  @atdd-loop-doors-family
  Scenario: Judge a family program on every listed instance and check its fit on instances it was not fitted on
    Given eight bounded-counter instances generated by the instantiation tool, three of them marked for fitting
    When the family door completes the hole per instance and fits a linear form in the family parameter
    Then every instance is judged by transform check with its receipt replayed
    And the fitted program is checked again on all eight instances, five of them not fitted on
    And the coverage is stated as the checked instances, never all sizes
    And a program transfers to every instance directly or by its parameter-near constants

  @stage-1b
  @atdd-loop-doors-meanings
  Scenario: Search a sketch's meanings and key programs by what they mean
    Given sketches with several holes, some alone on their route and some compared with hole-free expressions
    When the sketch door solves them
    Then a hole alone on its route is derived exactly by itself and the others are branched over effect classes
    And the search over meanings completes the sketches the joint search completes and states the same verdicts
    And a candidate that would overflow signed 64-bit arithmetic is skipped and a large constant is derived exactly
    And two programs get equal meaning keys exactly when transform check finds them equivalent
